    "id": "p14-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Show that $x^2-8x+19>0$ for all $x\\in\\mathbb R$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x^2-8x+19=(x-4)^2+3\\ge3>0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2-8x+19&=(x^2-8x+16)-16+19\\\\x^2-8x+19&=(x-4)^2+3\\\\x^2-8x+19&\\ge3\\\\x^2-8x+19&>0\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis holds for all real $x$ because $(x-4)^2\\ge0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
